  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R3-023$qb$, $qb$A6-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Several people are waiting for your work and you feel pressure to send it before the final check. Demand is sustained, and quality failures would create significant downstream work. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Complete the critical check, communicate the realistic timing, and then send accurate work$qb$, $qb$Tell people you need a little more time for the final check$qb$, $qb$Send it now and check it afterward$qb$, $qb$Skip the check because several people are waiting$qb$, $qb$Send it without saying the check was skipped$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
