  ($qb$ITEM-SJT-2416$qb$, $qb$A6-04$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$Every new vendor review requires the same evidence-request email, folder structure and reviewer checklist to be assembled manually. What do you do?$qb$, $qb$Use an approved vendor-review template or workflow that creates the standard package and allows controlled case-specific additions.$qb$, $qb$Respond to vendor review requires the same evidence-request with the standard explanation before clarifying the other person's actual need.$qb$, $qb$Add more detail about vendor review requires the same evidence-request even though the problem is relevance or clarity rather than missing information.$qb$, $qb$Ask another colleague to take over vendor review requires the same evidence-request without preserving the context already available.$qb$, $qb$Treat the concern about vendor review requires the same evidence-request as resistance and continue with the original message.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
